From 5b2e38c422de9dc27a56efae195082e0776cf9a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Calvarro Nelson <jacalvar@microsoft.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Apr 2026 10:03:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Blazor] Add Blazor WebAssembly Service Defaults template
 (#64807)

* Add Blazor WebAssembly Service Defaults template

Add a new project template 'blazor-wasm-servicedefaults' for creating
service defaults libraries for Blazor WebAssembly applications with
.NET Aspire integration.

Features:
- OpenTelemetry support (logging, metrics, and tracing)
- Service discovery integration
- HTTP resilience with standard resilience handler
- Uses standard OpenTelemetry OTLP exporter

New files:
- BlazorWasmServiceDefaults-CSharp template content
- Template configuration and localization files (14 languages)
- Template test and baseline configuration
- Package version definitions for OpenTelemetry and Extensions packages

* Add --hosted flag to Blazor WebAssembly service defaults template

- Add 'hosted' boolean parameter to template.json for hosted vs standalone scenarios
- In hosted mode: config flows via BrowserConfiguration DOM comment (no JS initializer needed)
- In standalone mode: adds BlazorClientServerExtensions placeholder for config endpoint
- Remove commented-out component metrics/tracing (clean up template output)
- Add BlazorWasmServiceDefaultsTemplate_HostedAsync test for --hosted variant

* Fix blazor-wasm-servicedefaults template for test infrastructure

- Add dotnetcli.host.json to map skipRestore -> --no-restore (required by test infra)
- Add ide.host.json for IDE support
- Update template.json TFM from net10.0 to net11.0 (post-rebase fix)
- Update localized strings for net11.0 and hosted parameter
- Add #pragma warning disable xUnit1041 to test file (matches other template tests)

* Update blazor-wasm-servicedefaults template with OTLP exporters and telemetry

- Add WebAssembly-compatible OTLP exporters for traces, metrics, and logs
- Add protobuf serializers for OTLP wire format
- Add TaskBasedBatchExportProcessor for async-safe batching in WASM
- Use OTEL_SERVICE_NAME from configuration with project name fallback
- Add HTTP instrumentation filter to prevent OTLP feedback loops
- Add resilience handler and runtime instrumentation
- Create direct HttpClient instances to avoid IHttpClientFactory reentrancy
- Add JS initializer for standalone WASM config fetch
- Exclude wwwroot/ when hosted (framework handles DOM config)
- Update template-baselines.json with new files

* Add BrowserConfiguration for server-to-browser config via DOM comment

Introduces a BrowserConfiguration model that flows serializable options
from the server to the Blazor client via a <!--Blazor-Configuration:{}-->
HTML comment. This replaces the WebAssemblySettingsEmitter with a unified
mechanism that works across all render modes (Server, WebAssembly, Auto).

- BrowserConfiguration, ServerBrowserOptions, SsrBrowserOptions,
  WebAssemblyBrowserOptions model classes
- WithBrowserConfiguration() endpoint convention builder extension
- ConfigureBrowser component and HttpContext extensions
- EmitBrowserConfigurationOnce in EndpointHtmlRenderer
- TypeScript: discoverBrowserConfiguration() and Boot.Web.ts integration
  that applies config to logLevel, circuit, SSR, and WebAssembly options
